{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Annie is playing a game where she starts with a row of positive integers, written on a blackboard, each of which is a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. On each turn, she can erase two adjacent numbers and replace them with a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is greater than either of the erased numbers. This shortens the row of numbers, and she continues to take turns until only one number remains. Annie wins the game if the final remaining number is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the sum of the original numbers. Is it always possible for Annie to win, regardless of the starting row of numbers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rwYBDVE5sAg\">https://youtu.be/rwYBDVE5sAg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start by realizing that the algorithm of combining the smallest term with its smallest neighbor seems to work, and we attempt to prove that this algorithm yields a sum which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb0bdabf7b612c39300177581e1f69f117f31c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le 4\\cdot(\\text{the original sum})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We proceed with strong induction with the base cases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> our result is trivial and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> if the two numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, the combined term will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d4475792083d18a89504065c2bd41b4b59c5e87b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\max(x_1,x_2)\\le 2(x_1+x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />).\n</p><p>Denote the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8611d4e8c63115e73d79ad945af0ba16d13d5a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,\\dots,x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"11\" />, and let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/2576f17e9562051d0a523b8aa56258f2d2af9348.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=2x_1+4x_2+4x_3+4x_4+\\cdots+4x_{n-2}+4x_{n-1}+2x_n.\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We attempt to prove that our result is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dc124f5c4aa867e38b324ec00f20cbccc2db38e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the first index such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb9f355a4a1940e2016c73d5fc25f3d291fd9c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x_1+4x_2+\\cdots+4x_{k-1}+4x_k=S_k\\ge \\frac{S}{2},\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"37\" />\nand assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dcf0a88d61acc2d0df2e37f4e5057f1fd9012c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ne 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>WLOG, we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7083ff24c02225368cc8f080bc666a761461a605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k-2x_k\\le \\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"39\" />, as if not we can just mirror the sequence as both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae87113d0080603e213ea99c033a80b2e5a83e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k-2x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/5662bfbe4275296c4ed24ed14b6f3955048d10da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-S_{k-1}-2x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> cannot be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f6787208a24344f0b7f124daffd2ed65d16101a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"18\" height=\"39\" />, which contradicts our initial definition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By our inductive hypothesis, as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc5eba74ca038fb92c9cd22ac509b29e5c5e1db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_k-2x_k=2x_1+4x_2+\\cdots+4x_{k-1}+2x_k,\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"16\" />\nwe know we can combine the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> to form an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9530fa66c7d7fc6297699f974677197735d711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"39\" />, and similarly, as we know that the terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191ef26bc72336cc70cc3ebe81e035852ced438a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed an integer\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a84931ee2d97c06052c6369a96e997d770a22b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\le 2x_{k+1}+4x_{k+2}+\\cdots+4x_{n-1}+2x_n\\le S-S_k\\le \\frac{S}{2},\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"37\" />\nimplying that the combination of both terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba54f0e21632cbd36e3aafa6f105a8af8ba3ddf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>In the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce7f2c8cac20b2e92da94b9f7f38542e36c9973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> (or if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> we just mirror the entire sequence), we consider the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> terms, and as we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecddcd689d2153403fc0eed721e48ae332ba3788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1}-2x_{n-1}\\le \\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"39\" />, we can combine the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> terms to a value which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b9530fa66c7d7fc6297699f974677197735d711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>As we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b8632e4285c75d9f1b687b5300145d7bcd13f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n\\le \\frac{S}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"39\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f7bbd491c159aeccd9e2118ef4f2aae8ba6088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\ge 2x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />) we know that we can combine both terms to form a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba54f0e21632cbd36e3aafa6f105a8af8ba3ddf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~EaglesNRavens\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/5829e3a89bbdd272499085aef1efc31980ff0f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = (x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4ec6a0bc231c624ed5f1763cf4389a6066ea91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i, x_i \\in \\{2^k \\mid k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"22\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469a03c39430913e5188c998942851def663f719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S =\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"83\" height=\"53\" />. \n</p><p>Define the adjacent merge operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24dea7af5586c86415a2c4a334c851b37a25f424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega(a, b) = 2\\max(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Sequential adjacent applications of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51e96fb494f7122ef98fd6a63bd890dafefaeafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\iff$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /> Construction of a full alphabetic (left-to-right) binary tree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88fd35d37995a6687f4c4dfad0d9d54760ca455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall \\text{ leaf } i \\in T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2ce4362da4ca00165e88861d0e26e78d2c72e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{value} = x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b02c71989c89afda36a4e93b48a9e456f8e8a6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{depth} = d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c9c3991dbd1c9501fedee691497cd651b8ddd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall \\text{ internal node with children } u, v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"248\" height=\"18\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e7bc0eda068555ff0445fc985553220134317f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{value} = \\omega(u,v) = \\max(2u, 2v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>By induction, the root value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is given by:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/9684000d303f16238059e92e6d942ed1f4ee1628.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = \\max_{1 \\le i \\le n} (x_i 2^{d_i})\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"29\" />\nWinning condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6bb0e2b33c93032ed43d0a584e6a621ea08a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W \\iff \\exists \\text{ valid tree } T \\text{ such that } R &lt; 4S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"316\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b024de2960a98c52ccb3c9919e8efc6c66f09fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because \\forall i, x_i \\in \\{2^k\\} \\land \\text{closure of } \\omega \\implies R \\in \\{2^k \\mid k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"404\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19151d066f51abbd17ee502e7f4cf058ee4bdb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\max \\{2^k \\mid 2^k &lt; 4S, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"244\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\because R \\in \\{2^k\\} \\implies W &amp;\\iff R \\le M \\\\\n&amp;\\iff \\forall i, \\, x_i 2^{d_i} \\le M \\\\\n&amp;\\iff \\forall i, \\, 2^{d_i} \\le \\frac{M}{x_i} \\\\\n&amp;\\iff \\forall i, \\, d_i \\le \\log_2 M - \\log_2 x_i\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c71006aa513bb1188c01c00100084c9407d52c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_i = \\log_2 M - \\log_2 x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"19\" />. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90ba4a42128cd79a7ee44114bf91537850aaaef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because M, x_i \\in \\{2^k\\} \\implies L_i \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"22\" />). \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751e928356edf89e364f29a5e201b4ccd2184067.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies W \\iff \\exists \\text{ alphabetic binary tree } T \\text{ where } \\forall i, d_i \\le L_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"450\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Evaluate the Kraft sum constraint for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c2601e8ed1379276d3289d6881f139749d1f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{L_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf03b7366df523526dde8ff6fb4ee69eae8b803.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n 2^{-L_i} = \\sum_{i=1}^n 2^{-\\log_2(M/x_i)} = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\frac{x_i}{M} = \\frac{S}{M}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"47\" />\nBy definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0417ae1c0aaddd6b6ee53a43b3a6b84081410898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M &lt; 4S \\le 2M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a0cc124341c560287ec4844222c3a7ded9d2d13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{1}{4} &lt; \\frac{S}{M} \\le \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\sum_{i=1}^n 2^{-L_i} \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed447db12c859bda7cff8fa1fac15cab0661dfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q_i = 2^{-L_i+1} = 2 \\cdot 2^{-L_i} \\implies\\sum_{i=1}^n q_i = 2 \\sum_{i=1}^n 2^{-L_i} \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"397\" height=\"53\" />. \n</p><p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed21411c5f8c563e0e67e7e47d29c98172045e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1 = 0, C_{i+1} = C_i + q_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />, and intervals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9cb6661f77657c1ded3f90ba0e9b01f6de87663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_i = [C_i, C_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18ae8bebc46a95880923c30c57018d5ec2f39539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because\\sum q_i \\le 1 \\implies \\forall i, I_i \\subseteq [0, 1] \\land (i \\neq j \\implies I_i \\cap I_j = \\emptyset)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"447\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p>Notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86deea745954bff1ced3d816e9ab660baa0c3df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|I_i| = 2 \\cdot 2^{-L_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"22\" />. By the fundamental property of dyadic intervals:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea46b4ec734b349dc7b6a1a4f09dc16c64396d52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\forall I \\text{ with } |I|=2\\cdot 2^{-L}, \\exists \\text{ sub-interval } J = [k \\cdot 2^{-L}, (k+1) \\cdot 2^{-L}) \\subseteq I, \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"20\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2eff020e0bb1cfdeabf57da40d56292c98ca1ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_i = \\lceil C_i \\cdot 2^{L_i} \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" />, and define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765a47828543c6eaa78d32d47ebb8f6635adb67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J_i = [k_i \\cdot 2^{-L_i}, (k_i+1) \\cdot 2^{-L_i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n&amp;\\implies J_i \\subseteq I_i \\\\\n&amp;\\because I_i \\cap I_j = \\emptyset \\land \\text{strictly ordered left-to-right} \\implies J_i \\cap J_j = \\emptyset \\land \\text{strictly ordered} \\\\\n&amp;\\because J_i = [k_i 2^{-L_i}, (k_i+1)2^{-L_i}) \\iff \\text{Unique binary prefix string of length } L_i \\\\\n&amp;\\implies \\{J_i\\}_{i=1}^n \\text{ forms a valid alphabetic prefix code} \\\\\n&amp;\\implies \\exists \\text{ binary tree } T' \\text{ with initial nodes } x_i \\text{ at strict depth } L_i\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/719a4425b8d0382c16c233a2f7d3d8b97bbe750b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = \\text{Prune}(T&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" /> (recursively eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392d141b4ed58f72205291574368a2b98ec2114e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{degree-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> internal nodes, redirecting child to parent). \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc00d80594b8bf93517e5d1caa43458435b36e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies T \\text{ is a full alphabetic binary tree}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84c1010d6065287a68005ed71c34d84f3246735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\because \\text{Pruning strictly decreases or maintains depth without violating left-to-right order}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"613\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f39e09d921fd329b2d4f3bb4e046a02881ba6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\forall i \\in T, \\text{ final depth } d_i \\le L_i      \\implies R = \\max_{i=1}^n (x_i 2^{d_i}) \\le \\max_{i=1}^n (x_i 2^{L_i}) = M &lt; 4S      \\implies W \\text{ is mathematically guaranteed}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"921\" height=\"32\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~funkCCP\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.o